This is a remote position.
On behalf of our Client, a global consulting company which is building their new SAP implementation teams in Poland, we are looking for experienced SAP PP and/or QM Principal Consultants , who will work on implementation and transformation projects. In the role, you will:

• Manage full life cycle implementations of SAP S/4HANA in area of Production Planning & Manufacturing Execution and/or Quality Management;

• Evaluate business requirements, identify relevant SAP capabilities and apply best practices;

• Plan, prepare and execute Fit-Gap / Fit-to-Standard Workshops;

• Do Solution Design & Adoption for identified GAPs and business process improvement measures;

• Ensure system implementation;

• Be sparring partner for the client and have project management responsibilities.

Our Client is a mid-size management consulting firm from the UK, specialized in implement transformational and innovative SAP solutions for the worlds’ largest organisations, recognized in the market for their client innovations and dedicated training and career paths they offer to their consultants. Thanks to that your career will never stop, and the company's values and trusted relationships with their clients and among all their team members will bring you to the next level of SAP consulting world, while thanks to REMOTE style of work you will be able to maintain work-live balance and have an unbreakable satisfaction from your work.
Requirements

• Higher education degree in Economics, Information Technology or equivalent;

• At least 2-5 Full Project Lifecycles of work experience in SAP PP and/or QM, the more the better;

• Profound Production Planning & Shop-Floor Manufacturing Execution and/or Quality Management process experience combined with the ability to translate business requirements into system design specifications;

• S/4HANA project experience and/or certification;

• Preferably experienced in international template rollout projects;

• Efficient and communicative team player and self-starter.

Benefits

• REMOTE work in European implementation and transformation projects;

• Limited traveling, only when really needed;

• Industry-leading compensation and benefits;

• Working with latest SAP technologies;

• Exposure to strategic projects, where you’ll be able to see your own ideas transform into breakthrough results;

• Being an important part of a diverse and talented consulting team;

• Work in an innovation-driven practice and a high-performance culture;

• Top training and development opportunities;

• True possibility to grow your career and achieve your personal ambitions.

