Senior Implementation Consultant, Logis Dispatch &nbsp;

Team: Implementation, Logis · Level: Senior Implementation Consultant · Reports to: Team Lead, Implementation (Logis Dispatch) · Location: Remote, United States &nbsp;

Outcome. Dispatch centers go live on Logis Dispatch on the planned date, right the first time, and trust the system from the first call. &nbsp;

About the role &nbsp;

A dispatch center cannot stop to go live. When we implement Logis Dispatch, we change the system a center uses to send help to every call, on a floor that runs 24 hours a day. A good go-live is quiet. A bad one is felt on the next emergency. &nbsp;

You lead our most complex Logis Dispatch implementations from kickoff to handoff: discovery of how the center works today, configuration, interfaces, data, training, and the cutover itself. You are the senior voice on the team, the one others come to when a project gets hard. &nbsp;

Where we are headed &nbsp;

Logis Dispatch is growing across North America and Europe, and into new kinds of customers such as mobile integrated health programs. The product is moving to the cloud and the browser, which will change how fast a center can go live. &nbsp;

You will lead the projects that set the standard, and help design the faster way we will implement next. &nbsp;

Who ESO is &nbsp;

ESO is the first responder for the first responders. We build software and data products for EMS agencies, fire departments, hospitals, and government stakeholders, and serve more than 18,000 customers. Our mission is to improve community health and safety outcomes through the power of data. &nbsp;

How you support the mission &nbsp;

You support the mission by making sure dispatchers can trust the system in front of them from the first call after cutover. When a center goes live well, crews get to calls faster and leaders can see what is working. &nbsp;

You support your team by setting the standard: you follow the playbook, improve it, and help newer consultants run their first go-lives. &nbsp;

What you will do &nbsp;

Lead each implementation &nbsp;

• Own a set of Logis Dispatch implementations, including the largest and most complex, each on a dated plan in the project management platform with health, risks, and next steps current every week. &nbsp;

• Run discovery with the center: call types, response plans, units and stations, geography, and the workflows of call-takers, dispatchers, and supervisors. &nbsp;

• Raise risks early to your team lead and the customer, with a plan to recover. &nbsp;

Configure, connect, and cut over &nbsp;

• Configure Logis Dispatch to the configuration standards, including mapping and unit recommendations. &nbsp;

• Work with Integration Engineering on interfaces: ePCR, billing, mapping and vehicle location, telephony, and paging. &nbsp;

• Plan and run the cutover with the center, often on site, with a rollback plan and a go or no-go call. &nbsp;

Train, hand off, and raise the bar &nbsp;

• Train call-takers, dispatchers, supervisors, and administrators on the workflows they will use every shift. &nbsp;

• Hand off cleanly at go-live: Logis Dispatch support in Customer Care owns tickets, and Customer Success owns the relationship. &nbsp;

• Mentor newer consultants and keep the implementation playbook current with what each project teaches us. &nbsp;

Time tracking &nbsp;

• Log your time in real time, as you finish each issue or task, in the time tracking system, by customer and type of work. &nbsp;

How success is measured &nbsp;

• Go-lives on the date in the project plan, and right the first time, with no serious incident caused by the setup in the first 30 days. &nbsp;

• Time to value: days from kickoff to the center running live calls in Logis Dispatch, against the standard for the project size. &nbsp;

• Every project plan current each week: dates, health, and next steps. &nbsp;

• Customer satisfaction (CSAT) at go-live and at handoff. &nbsp;

